            <ArticleTitle>Splenic abscess after sleeve gastrectomy: a report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>635-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Partial demarcation and infarction of the upper pole of the spleen is not a rare occurrence after laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG). However, development of an abscess in the absence of leakage is extremely rare.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We present herein two unusual case reports of splenic abscess in patients following LSG.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
